{'symbol': 'MET', 'date': '2021-08-24 16:45:00', 'title': 'METLIFE INVESTMENT MANAGEMENT ORIGINATES $6.4 BILLION IN PRIVATE PLACEMENT DEBT AND PRIVATE STRUCTURED CREDIT FOR 1H 2021', 'text': "WHIPPANY, N.J.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--METLIFE INVESTMENT MANAGEMENT (MIM), THE INSTITUTIONAL ASSET MANAGEMENT BUSINESS OF METLIFE, INC. (NYSE: MET), TODAY ANNOUNCED IT ORIGINATED $6.4 BILLION IN PRIVATE PLACEMENT DEBT AND PRIVATE STRUCTURED CREDIT FOR THE FIRST HALF OF 2021 ACROSS 107 TRANSACTIONS. THIS INCLUDED $1.2 BILLION OF INVESTMENTS ORIGINATED ON BEHALF OF UNAFFILIATED INSTITUTIONAL CLIENTS. MIM'S TOTAL PRIVATE PLACEMENT DEBT AND PRIVATE STRUCTURED CREDIT ASSETS UNDER MANAGEMENT STOOD AT $102"}{'symbol': 'MET', 'date': '2021-08-24 08:30:00', 'title': "FROM MAN'S BEST FRIEND TO BUDGET BUSTER: PET PARENTS SEEK SUPPORT AS THEY PREPARE FOR A RETURN TO IN-PERSON WORK", 'text': "NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- #EMPLOYEEBENEFITS--AS MILLIONS OF EMPLOYEES ACROSS THE U.S. ANTICIPATE A POTENTIAL RETURN TO IN-PERSON WORK, THOSE WHO ARE PET PARENTS—INCLUDING MANY WHO PARTICIPATED IN THE MORE THAN 2 MILLION ADOPTIONS OF DOGS AND CATS FROM SHELTERS LAST YEAR2—HAVE SOME ADDITIONAL CONCERNS BEYOND MISSING THEIR FAVORITE FURRY COLLEAGUE. ACCORDING TO METLIFE PET INSURANCE'S NEW PET PARENT PULSE SURVEY, THREE IN FOUR (74 PERCENT) WORKING PET PARENTS ARE THINKING ABOUT PET CARE COSTS DURING THIS TRANSITIO"}